@HostAddress = http://localhost:8081
@Token = Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

# Credentials come from your local .env file (never hard-code them here).
# Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension, which reads .env via $dotenv.

### === HEALTH ===

### Health (expect 200 Healthy; sqlserver Unhealthy -> 503; kafka down -> "Degraded")
GET {{HostAddress}}/health


### === AUTH ===

### Login as the seeded admin (run first; other requests reuse its token)
# @name login
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_SEED_USERNAME}}",
  "password": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD}}"
}

### Register a user (expect 201; run twice -> 409)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Same name, different case (expect 409: usernames are case-insensitive)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ALICE",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Make a user a Merchant (admin only)
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/user
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 2,
  "role": "Merchant"
}

### Refresh (paste a refresh token from a login response)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "paste-a-refresh-token-here"
}


